<%# How often life emerged in each arm of one sweep, against the same sweep's control arm.
    This is the sweep's own outcome and not the plateau the hypothesis above turns on: no
    verdict on this page reads it, and it is printed once per sweep rather than once per
    observable. %>
<h3>How often life emerged</h3>
<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" id="<%= bet.slug %>-emergence-rates"
     aria-label="How often life emerged in each arm of the <%= bet.slug %> sweep">
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Arm</th>
        <th class="numeric">Terminal runs</th>
        <th class="numeric">Emerged</th>
        <th class="numeric">Rate</th>
        <th class="numeric">Against the control</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% bet.arms.each do |arm| %>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <span class="mono"><%= arm.label %></span>
            <% if arm.control? %><span class="badge badge-info">control</span><% end %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.terminal_count %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.emerged_count %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono">
            <% if arm.tested? %>
              <%= arm.emergence_fraction %>
              (<%= number_to_percentage(arm.emergence_rate * 100, precision: 0) %>)
            <% else %>
              —
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono">
            <% p_value = bet.emergence_p_value(arm) %>
            <% if p_value.nil? %>
              —
            <% else %>
              p = <%= number_with_precision(p_value, precision: 2, significant: true,
                                            strip_insignificant_zeros: true) %>
              <% if bet.emergence_significant?(arm) %>
                <span class="badge badge-warning">p &lt; 0.05</span>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p><strong><%= bet.emergence_reading %></strong></p>
<p class="text-sm text-muted">
  One row per arm of the same sweep. "Terminal runs" counts the runs of the arm that reached
  an end with at least one sample, "Emerged" the confirmed crossings among them, and "Rate"
  the second over the first. "Against the control" is a two-sided Fisher exact test of the
  arm's emerged and unemerged runs against the control arm's — a dash for the control arm
  itself and for an arm with nothing terminal to test. The test describes how often life
  emerged under each substrate and decides nothing about the plateau above.
</p>
